    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/agent/telemetry_retention.py a file is a raw serving receipt candidate only when its name matches the raw pattern and its first parseable row's job_id field equals the job id parsed from the name. A file failing either test is never listed eligible and never deleted, and the listing reports it as not a raw receipt. The module docstring no longer claims a request receipt carries no job id, and states the row check instead. Tests in tests/test_telemetry_retention.py assert that a file named requests-2026-10-01.jsonl holding router request rows is not a candidate, and that a file named deepseek-v4-1-flash-1278105.jsonl whose first row carries job_id 1278999 is not a candidate. Gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_retention.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status; any evidence fragment written ends with a trailing newline",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make retire-raw treat a file as a raw serving receipt only when its first row carries the job id its name claims",
